{
  "note": [
    "The Tower Core's fabric (DR-113), cut from the one tower layout in scripts/fabric-tower.mjs, where all six rooms of the tower top are placed once in the core's frame -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. Every number of the room itself is the hand cut of DR-063 unchanged, part for part, because TOWER-CORE.metadata.json v3 and the Upper Elevator's, Comm Room's, Observation Deck's and Helipad's packages all quote it: a drum of radius 3.4 and height 4.2 in 56 segments, concrete on a concrete-worn floor, gaps at -19..19 (the elevator door), 32..58 (north-east to the Comm Room) and 212..238 (south-west to the Observation Deck), each headed at 2.5; the trim frame and the plate-steel leaf at the north door; the stair from [-2.2, 0.06, 1.05] to [-2.2, 4.1, -1.05] with its column; the cool lamp at [0, 4.05, 0] and the warm one at [1.9, 2.5, -1.9].",
    "What is new is only what is through the three gaps. North, the Upper Elevator's car at its upper stop, its wall against the drum's -- 3.8 x 3.1 x 3.4, its ceiling fitting and the control panel on its east wall (UPPER-ELEVATOR v4); its interior shows whenever UPPER-ELEVATOR-DOOR has OPENBIT, and the car is always there, because the exit itself refuses the walk when it is not (rules/connectors.js). North-east, a plain passage 0.80 m deep and then the Comm Room (COMM-ROOM v2, an octagon on the tower's own 45-degree axis): its floor, its far north-east wall 10.8 m off and the cable trunk climbing that wall into the ceiling. NOT the consoles and NOT the red lamp, though TOWER-CORE v3's COMM-PASSAGE says they show -- the passage's far end is 1.5 m wide at 4.32 m, which holds every ray inside 9.85 degrees of the axis, and the nearest console stands 2.5 m off it. South-west, straight through the drum's thickness onto the Observation Deck -- the terrace, the parapet at 11.5 m and, over its coping, the sea 500 m below: the room's only daylight, and the only thing in it that changes with the hour.",
    "UP is not drawn. TOWER-CORE v3's wallOpenings.STAIR-HEAD puts a 1.2 m opening in the ceiling at [-2.2, 3.9, 0] with the Helipad's daylight coming down it, but the kit's `drum` lays its ceiling as one disc and cannot pierce it, and cutting the hole means replacing accepted fabric. Left as the hand cut has it and reported instead: the stair climbs to a solid ceiling here, and the shaft above it is in the Helipad's scene."
  ],
